title ALES90 — Lotus's DC-offset remover, the pure translation that undoes the offset the even-harmonic family introduces
prompt recur baton prin — continue the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux-first lap, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates
think The dead-zone trilogy closed at ALES89, and the ALES89 design doc itself BOOKED the next Lotus crux: the DC blocker that removes the offset the rectifiers (ALES84/85/86) and the 1-bit crush (ALES81) introduce. Lindy-first, DC removal is a permanent staple of every audio chain — on every console channel, at the front of every codec, right after every nonlinearity — so it reads true for as long as audio is stored as signed samples. Crux-first within tier, it is the tool the family that JUST landed demands: the even-harmonic generators each shift the mean off zero, and nothing yet took that offset back out.
think Chose the BLOCK-MEAN remover over the one-pole IIR DC blocker for this lap. The IIR blocker (y[n] = x[n] − x[n−1] + R·y[n−1]) has a fractional feedback coefficient and wants a carried-state design and a stability bound of its own (the ALES43 shape) — a meatier round. The block-mean remover proves in pure integers with no float and no stability argument: sum the span in i64, subtract the truncated mean, saturate once. It undoes exactly the CONSTANT offset a rectifier or asymmetric clip introduces over a bounded region — the right first tool. Named the IIR blocker as the explicit later rung so the compass stays honest about what this rung is and is not.
think The defining invariant is that DC removal is a PURE TRANSLATION — the same constant leaves every sample — so it PRESERVES EVERY SAMPLE-TO-SAMPLE DIFFERENCE exactly (y[i] − y[j] = x[i] − x[j] where nothing saturates): only the mean moves, the waveform shape and all its AC content carried through untouched. That is the clean distinction from ALES2's gain, which SCALES the differences. The mean is truncated toward zero (@divTrunc, the suite's honest-lossy rule), which gives a provable residual bound |Σ y| < count (residual mean magnitude < 1 LSB), from which a zero-mean signal being unchanged and idempotence-where-nothing-saturates both fall straight out.
obs Followed the parametric-waveshaper pattern exactly (rectify.rye / infinite_clip.rye): module + design doc + witness + README status-line and rung-bullet sync + session log, one signed commit. Ten laws proven; the witness imports ALES84 and proves the composition crux beside the map (rectify a symmetric wave → sum 24000, a real DC offset → dc_remove restores |Σ| < count). Witness GREEN on the first run; tame_style_check bans clean and the new module carries no ratchet debt (many asserts, snake_case, no @memcpy, i64 accumulation, one saturate reused from ALES2). Empty span is a clean no-op (no divide by zero); BadRange refuses before any read or write.
loom witness=ales_dc_remove_witness selftest=GREEN laws=10 module_lines=205
file lotus/dc_remove.rye the DC-offset remover, y = saturate(x − mean), a pure translation preserving every difference, residual mean < 1 LSB, ten laws proven
file tools/ales_dc_remove_witness.rish builds the module, runs the selftest, asserts the single GREEN ales-dc-remove line
file active-designing/20260814-222356_fill-ales90-lotus-dc-offset-remover.md the self-approved design read naming the crux, the pure-translation invariant, the rectifier composition, and the ten laws
file lotus/README.md front-door status line and rung bullet synced with ALES90, stamp refreshed
recommend keep-going the offset-generating family and the tool that clears it now stand together; the loop names its own next Lotus crux — the one-pole IIR DC blocker (a drifting-offset remover with carried state, the ALES43 shape), a hysteresis comparator that gives ALES89's square a memory against chatter, or a fresh DSP family — as its own self-approved design round
